{
  "dom_id": "step-e9969",
  "name": "Example: Solving Equations Using the Power and Quotient Rules",
  "problem": "Solve the equation $\\log_2 (4x) - 2\\log_2\\left(x^2\\right) = 1.$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the logarithms share the same base. \n\nFirst, we apply the power rule to the first term to make the coefficient in front of each logarithm the same:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{2}⁡(4x)-2{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})=1 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(4x)-{log}_{2}⁡({({x}^{2})}^{2})=1 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(4x)-{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{4}) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we combine the logarithms using the quotient rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{4x}{{x}^{4}}) & =1 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting this equation in its equivalent exponential form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}} & ={2}^{1} \\\\ \\frac{4}{{x}^{3}} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve this rational equation for $x$ using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}} & =2 \\\\ {x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{{x}^{3}} & ={x}^{3}\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\cancel{{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\cancel{{x}^{3}}} & =2{x}^{3} \\\\ 2{x}^{3} & =4 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =2 \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now check for an extraneous solution by substituting back into the original equation: \n\nSubstituting $x=\\sqrt[3]{2}$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{2}⁡(4(\\sqrt[3]{2}))-2{log}_{2}⁡((\\sqrt[3]{2})^{2}) & \\overset{?}{=}1 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(4(\\sqrt[3]{2}))-{log}_{2}⁡{((\\sqrt[3]{2})^{2})}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}1 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(4(\\sqrt[3]{2}))-{log}_{2}⁡((\\sqrt[3]{2})^{4}) & \\overset{?}{=}1 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(4(\\sqrt[3]{2}))-{log}_{2}⁡(2(\\sqrt[3]{2})) & \\overset{?}{=}1 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{4\\sqrt[3]{2}}{2\\sqrt[3]{2}}) & \\overset{?}{=}1 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{4\\cancel{\\sqrt[3]{2}}}{2\\cancel{\\sqrt[3]{2}}}) & \\overset{?}{=}1 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{4}{2}) & \\overset{?}{=}1 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(2) & \\overset{?}{=}1 \\\\ 1 & =1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=\\sqrt[3]{2}$ is a valid solution.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-e9969\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n                 \n                <div class=\"example\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Example:</span> Solving Equations Using the Power and Quotient Rules</div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"e9969\">?</div>\n                    </div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                        <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-transition: none;\n                            -moz-transition: none;\n                            -ms-transition: none;\n                            -o-transition: none\n                            }\n\n                            .mjx-svg-href {\n                            fill: blue;\n                            stroke: blue\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox {\n                            display: table!important\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox span {\n                            display: table-cell!important;\n                            width: 10000em!important;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage__block {\n                            text-align: center;\n                            margin: 1em 0em;\n                            position: relative;\n                            display: block!important;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            width: 100%\n                            }</style><p>Solve the equation <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"26.165ex\" height=\"3.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -1.005ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -934.9 11265.4 1367.4\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\\log_2 (4x) - 2\\log_2\\left(x^2\\right) = 1.</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id